  "findings": {
    "visibility": "The original exhaustive startup HideObject trees can finish while actors are hidden. Saved VMs retain the hidden actor but no consumer remains after quest flags change on another map. Recovery derives and evaluates only terminating, acyclic, read-only conditional trees with visibility leaves. It refuses pending families, rewards, AddMob, removals, loops and waits, and does not recreate or reveal dead/recruited actors.",
    "direct_combat": "Contact previously forced hit=true for melee and free-aim projectiles. Contact now invokes ordinary Attack/Defence with aim penalties and original melee backstab conditions; arrows retain their launch damage and cannot acquire a melee backstab after a weapon change.",
    "revival": "Death-time portrait inspection persisted after living ownership returned. Spectating now ends when a living selected owned actor becomes available, including reliable revival events arriving before the living snapshot. First person resumes after the original stand-up clip.",
    "dialogue": "Clicked topics skipped the native 6064a0 walking stage. They now retain authored placement, then face actual positions. Dialogue and return walkers are protected from calm AI and direct-look heading; failed routes settle without the 30-second placement fallback.",
    "island_travel": "Previously visited original-campaign islands are selectable from the travel map. An excursion saves its actual departure zone and stable hero/mercenary/pet positions and facing. Return uses the normal zone VM/object save without rolling back current stats, inventory or quest flags. Bookmarks persist across saves and are consumed on arrival. The first visit back to an island without an excursion bookmark uses its previously visited main settlement. Temporary parties, captivity, blocked story actors, active dialogue, no-camp flags and in-progress cross-island transfers cannot use this route; authority rechecks at selection."
  },
